   "reason": "The gate lives in the repository it guards and the build runs the new gate, so a gate that dropped a check would pass its own change. The filing act rebuilds every commit touching the gate with its parent's gate and records whether that one would have refused; the commit that installs a gate has no parent gate and is recorded as ungated by construction, its clearance and Owner-Line checked after the fact. Lifts when piece 7's rule holds the gate's files.",
